# BotShieldHeuristicTrigger — illustrative reference for the compiled-
# in default rule set.
#
# This file is NOT a required include. mod_botshield ships these
# rules compiled into the module and seeds them into every server
# scope at post_config time, so the module Just Works with zero
# config. The file exists only so operators who want to see the
# defaults can read them in a familiar httpd.conf shape, and so
# operators tweaking behavior have a starting template.
#
# Heuristics are the cheap built-in score signals — UA / header
# patterns and first-sight Bloom-filter checks — that fire before
# any operator-configured trigger or rate-limit rule. Promoting them
# to a directive family means an operator can tune individual
# penalties, disable a single heuristic, or wipe the whole slate and
# build it back up from zero, all without recompiling the module.
#
# Syntax:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger <name>|all [reset] [action=<verb> args...]
#
# Names:
#   missing-ua       UA header absent or empty.
#   missing-al       Accept-Language header absent or empty.
#   scraper-ua       UA contains a known HTTP-library token (curl,
#                    Wget, python-requests, urllib, httpx, aiohttp,
#                    Go-http-client, okhttp, axios, scrapy, java,
#                    libwww, lwp-request, ...).
#   first-sight-ip   Client IP not seen in the rotating Bloom filter
#                    (cookieless / signature-mismatched requests
#                    only — sig-verified clients skip this signal).
#
# Action verbs (same as BotShieldFlagTrigger):
#   action=score add=N             (signed; SUM across matching entries)
#   action=tier_floor min=<tier>   (pass|silent|form|captcha; MAX)
#
# Reset:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger <name> reset           # clear that name
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger <name> reset action=...  # clear + redeclare
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger all reset              # wipe ALL entries,
#                                                    # defaults included
#
# Observe-mode (logs `<reason>:observe` instead of applying):
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger missing-ua action=score add=40 mode=observe

# --- Compiled-in defaults --------------------------------------------
# Conservative score adds — none of these alone is enough to cross
# the silent-tier threshold (default 20). Two together (a curl with
# no Accept-Language: 50 + 15 + 5 first-sight = 70) lands in form-
# PoW tier (>=50). The shape rewards "looks like a real browser" and
# costs "looks like a script."
BotShieldHeuristicTrigger missing-ua       action=score add=40
BotShieldHeuristicTrigger missing-al       action=score add=15
BotShieldHeuristicTrigger scraper-ua       action=score add=50
BotShieldHeuristicTrigger first-sight-ip   action=score add=5

# --- Common overrides ------------------------------------------------
#
# Clean slate — wipe every default and start from zero. Useful for
# environments where the operator wants the module to score ONLY on
# their own configured triggers / rate-limits, with no implicit
# behavior from the heuristics layer.
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger all reset
#
# Soften the missing-UA penalty (keep it as a signal but don't bump
# tier on its own):
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger missing-ua reset action=score add=10
#
# Disable scraper-UA matching entirely (e.g., when a legitimate API
# integration uses a Go-http-client UA):
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger scraper-ua reset
#
# Promote first-sight-ip from a small score nudge to a tier_floor.
# Every never-before-seen client lands in silent tier regardless of
# their other signals; verified passes graduate them out:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger first-sight-ip reset
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger first-sight-ip action=tier_floor min=silent
#
# Stage a tighter scraper-UA penalty in observe mode for one release
# before enforcing:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger scraper-ua action=score add=80 mode=observe
#   # logs `scraper-ua-<token>:observe` on every fire; replace
#   # mode=observe with no flag once the rate looks right.
#
# Multiple actions on the same heuristic accumulate (SUM for score,
# MAX for tier_floor). Example: keep the default +50 score AND add a
# tier_floor for an extra-strict deployment:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger scraper-ua action=tier_floor min=form
#   # combined effect: +50 score (default) AND tier floor at form
